 ### Code/Performance optimizations
 
 - **Launch guard for SAS defines (startup/load/Sevopedia):** Added a strict define-integrity check using one **int sentinel** and one **string sentinel**, validated at pre-game start, game start, save load, Sevopedia creation, and Sevopedia show. If a value is missing or mismatched, Python raises a **fatal error** with `actual` vs `expected` values and guidance to launch from a Windows shortcut. The game will be **unplayable if the config is incorrect**. Change in: [`SASDefineGuard.py`](/Assets/Python/SASDefineGuard.py). See also [Quick Install Guide](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Quick_Install_Setup_Guide.md#place-a-shortcut-of-the-mod-on-your-desktop).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5770+) **Lazy init and cache SAS defines** (e.g., in advisors) to `None` and then to their actual value once if cache is `None`. This prevents and **empricially fixes**  direct caching in init, that empirically causes **python-like crashy behaviour** (i.e. similar behaviour to when python code is changed during runtime) on XML SAS define change of a value (instead of no effect and requiring a restart for the change to take effect). See for example [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py)'s `initDefines` method.
 - **Fail-fast XML lookup hardening:** replaced `getInfoTypeForString(...)` calls (terrain/features/bonuses and similar tags) with `getInfoTypeOrFail(...)` (in [SASUtils.py](/Assets/Python/SASUtils.py)), so **missing/renamed XML tags raise explicit errors** instead of silently using invalid `-1` values. Notably allowed to detect and fix incorrect `getInfoTypeOrFail("DIRECTION_NORTH")` instead of correct `DirectionTypes.DIRECTION_NORTH` (in Planet Generator map), or incorrect `getInfoTypeOrFail("PLOT_PEAK")` failing instead of correct `PlotTypes.PLOT_PEAK` (in Peirce map).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5515+) **Merged** the **old split/interdependent Foreign Advisor** implementation from the two-file setup (`CvForeignAdvisor.py` + `CvExoticForeignAdvisor.py`) into a **single unified** [CvForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignAdvisor.py) with the **full tab set** (as of now Relations/Glance/Active/Bonus/Info/Tech/Cities). In our findings, **this was the only screen file** using that **interdependent split** pattern, so merging it into one file directly **fixes that inconsistency** and **reduces maintenance burden**; other major screen files such as [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py) and [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py) are lengthy but unified files. By contrast, true alternatives use independent variants (for example BUG/non-BUG [CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py) / [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py) paths), not interdependent split files.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5516+) **Remove screen-dependent geometry computation** from `__init__` in advisors because this advisor object is created before a reliable screen context exists; doing layout in `interfaceScreen` **ensures correct values for the current resolution**. Keeping **only screen-independent edge constants** in `__init__` ensures **no redundant recomputation** is made again in `interfaceScreen`, and **catches loud screen-dependent errors** in `__init__`.

